' Figure 4.6: Sequence Diagram – Real-Time Messaging & Showcase Workflow
@startuml
skinparam sequence {
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    ParticipantBorderColor #161311
    ActorBackgroundColor #FAF8F5
    ActorBorderColor #161311
    LifeLineBorderColor #161311
    ArrowColor #161311
}

actor "Team Member A" as MemberA
participant "React Client A" as ClientA
participant "Socket.IO Server\n(socket/index.js)" as SocketServer
participant "Express REST API\n(messageController)" as REST
database "MongoDB Database" as DB
participant "React Client B" as ClientB
actor "Team Member B" as MemberB

MemberA -> ClientA : Types chat message & hits Send
ClientA -> REST : POST /api/projects/:id/messages { message }
activate REST

REST -> REST : Verify JWT & isTeamMember(project, senderId)
REST -> DB : Message.create({ projectId, senderId, message })
activate DB
DB --> REST : Message saved with _id & timestamps
deactivate DB

REST -> SocketServer : getIo().to("project:<id>").emit("message:new", formattedMsg)
activate SocketServer
SocketServer -> ClientB : Broadcast "message:new" event
activate ClientB
ClientB --> MemberB : UI updates instantly with new message bubble
deactivate ClientB
deactivate SocketServer

REST --> ClientA : 201 Created { success: true, data: message }
deactivate REST
ClientA --> MemberA : Render sent message confirmation
@enduml
